1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,940
Seven days in Korea:

2
00:00:01,940 --> 00:00:03,860
a temple above the sea

3
00:00:03,860 --> 00:00:05,740
Gyeongju’s glowing pond

4
00:00:05,740 --> 00:00:07,600
Seoul’s palace and market food

5
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:10,080
in a route that makes the most of your week.

6
00:00:10,458 --> 00:00:13,018
Here is the route

7
00:00:13,018 --> 00:00:15,638
including one flexible day trip from Seoul.

8
00:00:16,164 --> 00:00:17,844
Three cities

9
00:00:17,844 --> 00:00:19,244
one memorable week.

10
00:00:20,214 --> 00:00:23,294
Book your KTX south ahead of time

11
00:00:23,294 --> 00:00:26,454
especially for weekends and holidays.

12
00:00:26,454 --> 00:00:28,534
Popular morning trains can fill up

13
00:00:28,534 --> 00:00:30,974
so check availability and book through the

14
00:00:30,974 --> 00:00:32,274
Korail website or app.

15
00:00:32,568 --> 00:00:35,128
Get a transit card when you arrive.

16
00:00:35,128 --> 00:00:37,668
It works on subways and buses in every city

17
00:00:37,668 --> 00:00:38,928
on this plan

18
00:00:38,928 --> 00:00:40,368
making local journeys simpler.

19
00:00:41,082 --> 00:00:44,682
Spend your first three days in Seoul.

20
00:00:44,682 --> 00:00:46,122
Stay somewhere central

21
00:00:46,122 --> 00:00:47,662
such as Myeongdong

22
00:00:47,662 --> 00:00:48,962
Jongno or City Hall

23
00:00:48,962 --> 00:00:52,062
so the main sights are a short ride away.

24
00:00:52,548 --> 00:00:54,388
On day one

25
00:00:54,388 --> 00:00:56,468
begin at Gyeongbokgung Palace

26
00:00:56,468 --> 00:00:59,308
then explore the traditional lanes of Bukchon

27
00:00:59,308 --> 00:01:02,528
and the shops and streets of Insadong.

28
00:01:02,528 --> 00:01:04,048
Finish with an evening walk beside

29
00:01:04,048 --> 00:01:05,588
Cheonggyecheon stream.

30
00:01:06,414 --> 00:01:09,849
Day two starts with breakfast at Gwangjang Market.

31
00:01:09,849 --> 00:01:10,664
After that

32
00:01:10,664 --> 00:01:13,517
browse Myeongdong’s shops and street food

33
00:01:13,517 --> 00:01:16,554
then head to N Seoul Tower for sunset.

34
00:01:17,472 --> 00:01:19,421
Keep day three flexible.

35
00:01:19,421 --> 00:01:23,320
Choose Hongdae and Yeonnam-dong for youth culture

36
00:01:23,320 --> 00:01:24,798
Seongsu for cafes

37
00:01:24,798 --> 00:01:27,957
Gangnam and Jamsil for the modern city

38
00:01:27,957 --> 00:01:30,072
or a Korean bathhouse.

39
00:01:30,426 --> 00:01:34,126
Choose one of these three options for day four.

40
00:01:34,126 --> 00:01:35,686
They are alternatives

41
00:01:35,686 --> 00:01:37,666
not a race to fit everything in.

42
00:01:38,244 --> 00:01:39,964
For the DMZ

43
00:01:39,964 --> 00:01:42,344
the border area with North Korea

44
00:01:42,344 --> 00:01:44,904
you must join an organised tour.

45
00:01:44,904 --> 00:01:46,884
Book ahead and bring your passport.

46
00:01:47,358 --> 00:01:49,898
Suwon is a good choice if you want to

47
00:01:49,898 --> 00:01:52,138
walk the walls of Hwaseong Fortress

48
00:01:52,138 --> 00:01:53,798
a UNESCO site.

49
00:01:53,798 --> 00:01:55,998
It is about an hour from Seoul by subway

50
00:01:55,998 --> 00:01:56,878
or train.

51
00:01:57,264 --> 00:02:00,008
Choose Nami Island for riverside walks.

52
00:02:00,008 --> 00:02:03,228
The article recommends it especially in autumn

53
00:02:03,228 --> 00:02:04,063
and winter

54
00:02:04,063 --> 00:02:07,584
when the island is a popular day-trip option.

55
00:02:08,178 --> 00:02:12,498
Take an early KTX from Seoul to Singyeongju Station.

56
00:02:12,498 --> 00:02:14,498
The ride takes about two to two and a

57
00:02:14,498 --> 00:02:15,698
half hours.

58
00:02:15,698 --> 00:02:18,438
Leave your bags at your hotel or a station locker.

59
00:02:20,532 --> 00:02:24,192
Gyeongju was the Silla kingdom’s capital for

60
00:02:24,192 --> 00:02:26,632
nearly a thousand years.

61
00:02:26,632 --> 00:02:28,672
Start at Bulguksa Temple

62
00:02:28,672 --> 00:02:31,472
then visit the grassy royal tombs and

63
00:02:31,472 --> 00:02:33,212
Cheomseongdae observatory.

64
00:02:33,534 --> 00:02:36,394
Stay into the evening for Donggung Palace and

65
00:02:36,394 --> 00:02:37,574
Wolji Pond

66
00:02:37,574 --> 00:02:39,374
lit up after dark.

67
00:02:39,374 --> 00:02:41,894
Gyeongju is quiet and lovely at night

68
00:02:41,894 --> 00:02:45,134
so stay here rather than rushing straight onward.

69
00:02:45,504 --> 00:02:46,581
From Gyeongju

70
00:02:46,581 --> 00:02:50,066
Busan is a short KTX journey from Singyeongju

71
00:02:50,066 --> 00:02:52,728
or about an hour by intercity bus.

72
00:02:52,728 --> 00:02:56,150
This route gives you two days for the coast

73
00:02:56,150 --> 00:02:58,604
markets and hillside streets.

74
00:02:58,962 --> 00:03:01,822
Start day six at Haedong Yonggungsa

75
00:03:01,822 --> 00:03:04,062
a temple beside the sea.

76
00:03:04,062 --> 00:03:06,822
Then spend midday at Haeundae Beach

77
00:03:06,822 --> 00:03:08,942
visit a Korean spa in Centum City

78
00:03:08,942 --> 00:03:10,822
and have dinner by the water.

79
00:03:11,172 --> 00:03:13,092
On day seven

80
00:03:13,092 --> 00:03:15,332
explore Gamcheon Culture Village and the

81
00:03:15,332 --> 00:03:17,412
Jagalchi fish market area

82
00:03:17,412 --> 00:03:19,092
then head home.

83
00:03:19,092 --> 00:03:22,572
Busan’s Gimhae Airport has international flights

84
00:03:22,572 --> 00:03:24,732
so you may not need to return to Seoul.

85
00:03:25,542 --> 00:03:27,882
If you fly from Incheon

86
00:03:27,882 --> 00:03:30,922
take the KTX back to Seoul and allow plenty

87
00:03:30,922 --> 00:03:33,202
of time to reach the airport.

88
00:03:33,202 --> 00:03:35,902
The train journey is about two and a half hours.

89
00:03:36,312 --> 00:03:39,366
The KTX connects the long-distance parts of

90
00:03:39,366 --> 00:03:40,444
this itinerary.

91
00:03:40,444 --> 00:03:43,438
Subways and buses handle most city travel

92
00:03:43,438 --> 00:03:46,972
and taxis are another option for short trips.

93
00:03:47,370 --> 00:03:48,780
From Incheon Airport

94
00:03:48,780 --> 00:03:52,390
take the airport train or a limousine bus into Seoul.

95
00:03:52,390 --> 00:03:53,406
For directions

96
00:03:53,406 --> 00:03:57,090
use Naver Map or KakaoMap rather than Google Maps.

97
00:03:57,420 --> 00:03:59,220
Pack light:

98
00:03:59,220 --> 00:04:01,680
you change hotels twice.

99
00:04:01,680 --> 00:04:03,440
Large bags can go in station lockers

100
00:04:03,440 --> 00:04:06,220
or you can send them between hotels with a

101
00:04:06,220 --> 00:04:07,420
luggage delivery service.

102
00:04:08,334 --> 00:04:12,554
Check entry rules for your passport before flying.

103
00:04:12,554 --> 00:04:14,054
For the day trip

104
00:04:14,054 --> 00:04:16,314
remember that the DMZ requires an organised

105
00:04:16,314 --> 00:04:18,194
tour and a passport.

106
00:04:18,648 --> 00:04:22,048
If a beach island and slower pace appeal more

107
00:04:22,048 --> 00:04:24,008
than the south-east

108
00:04:24,008 --> 00:04:26,908
swap days five to seven for Jeju.

109
00:04:26,908 --> 00:04:29,808
The plan there includes the west coast

110
00:04:29,808 --> 00:04:32,108
Sunrise Peak and Udo Island.

111
00:04:32,562 --> 00:04:35,822
Avoid these four common problems:

112
00:04:35,822 --> 00:04:37,982
cramming in too many cities

113
00:04:37,982 --> 00:04:40,262
leaving KTX tickets late

114
00:04:40,262 --> 00:04:41,282
missing a closing day

115
00:04:41,282 --> 00:04:44,142
and relying on Google Maps for directions.

116
00:04:44,820 --> 00:04:46,880
Keep the route simple:

117
00:04:46,880 --> 00:04:49,680
one city per travel day is enough.

118
00:04:49,680 --> 00:04:52,840
Book the train early for weekends and holidays

119
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:54,900
check palace and museum closing days before

120
00:04:54,900 --> 00:04:55,600
you go

121
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:58,340
and use a Korean map app for directions.

122
00:04:58,830 --> 00:05:00,010
Yes.

123
00:05:00,010 --> 00:05:02,730
A week is enough to see Seoul properly and

124
00:05:02,730 --> 00:05:05,070
visit one or two other places.

125
00:05:05,070 --> 00:05:06,730
With ten days or more

126
00:05:06,730 --> 00:05:08,950
you could add Jeju or Jeonju.

127
00:05:09,336 --> 00:05:13,056
Busan is a lively seaside city that is easy

128
00:05:13,056 --> 00:05:15,196
to reach by train.

129
00:05:15,196 --> 00:05:18,116
Jeju is a volcanic island with a slower pace

130
00:05:18,116 --> 00:05:18,856
more nature

131
00:05:18,856 --> 00:05:20,876
and a stronger need for a car.

132
00:05:21,402 --> 00:05:23,302
It is a good idea

133
00:05:23,302 --> 00:05:25,402
especially for weekends

134
00:05:25,402 --> 00:05:27,942
holidays and popular morning trains.

135
00:05:27,942 --> 00:05:30,282
Check availability and book through the Korail

136
00:05:30,282 --> 00:05:31,562
website or app.

137
00:05:32,268 --> 00:05:35,108
The plan is three days in Seoul

138
00:05:35,108 --> 00:05:36,108
one day trip

139
00:05:36,108 --> 00:05:37,448
one night in Gyeongju

140
00:05:37,448 --> 00:05:39,588
then two days in Busan.

141
00:05:39,588 --> 00:05:41,348
Book the KTX ahead

142
00:05:41,348 --> 00:05:41,868
travel light

143
00:05:41,868 --> 00:05:44,248
and leave room to enjoy each stop.

144
00:05:44,718 --> 00:05:45,873
The full guide

145
00:05:45,873 --> 00:05:48,485
with maps and links for every stop

146
00:05:48,485 --> 00:05:50,977
is free at Korea Plainly dot com.

147
00:05:50,977 --> 00:05:54,137
The link is at the top of the description.

148
00:05:54,137 --> 00:05:55,291
If this helped

149
00:05:55,291 --> 00:05:57,114
subscribe for more plain

150
00:05:57,114 --> 00:05:59,298
practical guides to Korea.

